DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbaacckkttrraaccee() function places into the array pointed by _a_d_d_r_l_i_s_t the
     array of the values of the program counter for each frame called up to
     _l_e_n frames.  The number of frames found (which can be fewer than _l_e_n) is
     returned.

     The bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss__ffmmtt() function takes an array of previously filled
     addresses from bbaacckkttrraaccee() in _a_d_d_r_l_i_s_t of _l_e_n elements, and uses _f_m_t to
     format them.  The formatting characters available are:

           a  The numeric address of each element as would be printed using
              %p.

           n  The name of the nearest function symbol (smaller than the ad‐
              dress element) as determined by dladdr(3) if the symbol was dy‐
              namic, or looked up in the executable if static and the /proc
              filesystem is available to determine the executable path.

           d  The difference of the symbol address and the address element
              printed using 0x%tx.

           D  The difference of the symbol address and the address element
              printed using +0x%tx if non-zero, or nothing if zero.

           f  The filename of the symbol as determined by dladdr(3).

     The array of formatted strings is returned as a contiguous memory address
     which can be freed by a single free(3).

     The bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss() function is equivalent of calling
     bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss__ffmmtt() with a format argument of %a <%n%D> at %f

     The bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss__ffdd() and bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss__ffdd__ffmmtt() are similar to
     the non _fd named functions, only instead of returning an array or
     strings, they print a new-line separated array of strings in fd, and re‐
     turn 0 on success and -1 on failure.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The bbaacckkttrraaccee() function returns the number of elements that were filled
     in the backtrace.  The bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss() and bbaacckkttrraaccee__ssyymmbboollss__ffmmtt()
     return a string array on success, and NULL on failure, setting _e_r_r_n_o.
     Diagnostic output may also be produced by the ELF symbol lookup func‐
     tions.

